  "text": "It's great that you want to make your mom a wonderful breakfast in bed! Making an omelette is a classic choice, and it's a flexible dish that everyone loves. Here's a simple recipe you can follow:\n\n**Materials you'll need:**\n- 2 eggs\n- A teaspoon of oil\n- Salt and pepper\n- Optional, chopped cheese\n- Optional, chopped vegetables or spices\n\n**Steps for making an omelette:**\n1. Beat the two eggs in a small bowl.\n2. Add salt and pepper to taste.\n3. Heat a bit of oil in a frying pan.\n4. Add the eggs to the pan over medium heat.\n5. Allow the edges to set, then use a fork to lift the edges and let the uncooked parts cook.\n6. Fold the omelette in half.\n7. Add cheese or vegetables if desired.\n8. Cook for a few more seconds, then flip the omelette.\n9. Serve with fresh fruit.\n\nThese instructions are simple for an easy learning experience. A small mess is okay. The idea is to make the omelette so that it looks as good as it tastes. You don't have to be perfect, just make something of value. Your mom will love it. Enjoy your cooking!",
